## Contextual reference data shown next to upgrade options.
const ENTRIES := {
	"resonance":{"title":"RESONANCE","text":"A meter earned by landing attacks and dodging through danger. At 100, press E, controller Y or BURST to unleash a Resonance Break: 135 damage, cleared enemy bullets and hazards, and brief protection. It is not a beat-timing requirement."},
	"stagger":{"title":"STAGGER","text":"Melee impact and abilities fill the thin gold bar beneath boss health. At 100, the boss is interrupted for 1.25 seconds and takes 30% extra damage. A seven-second lock prevents repeated permanent stuns."},
	"energy":{"title":"ENERGY","text":"Energy pays for your character ability and dodge. It regenerates over time; successful melee strikes restore more. Each character regenerates at a different rate. Maximum-energy upgrades increase the reserve, not regeneration speed."},
	"dodge":{"title":"DODGE / PERFECT DODGE","text":"Dodge moves you quickly and briefly prevents damage. It costs energy and has a recovery time. Actually passing through a harmful projectile or area attack earns a Perfect Dodge: resonance and style, once per dodge."},
	"parry":{"title":"PARRY / RIPOSTE","text":"Press L, controller LB or PARRY just before an enemy projectile touches you. The gold ring marks the active window. Bram, Vex and Aria destroy the shot and gain energy, resonance and stagger. Lyra reflects it. Aria also gains a 1.5-second riposte: her next melee strike deals 50% more damage. Beams, floor attacks and shockwaves cannot be parried."},
	"vitality":{"title":"VITALITY / DAMAGE","text":"Vitality is your health. Bram has 150, Vex 80, Aria 100 and Lyra 75 before upgrades. Character armor or vulnerability changes incoming damage. A hit grants a short protection period. Reaching zero ends a normal fight; tutorial checkpoints let you retry safely."},
	"melee":{"title":"MELEE / COMMITMENT","text":"Hold K, left mouse or STRIKE for your character's three-hit combo. The hammer is slow and powerful; knives are quick and short; the saber is balanced; the spear has reach but lower damage. A windup resolves later against the target's current location. Dodging can cancel it, retaining recovery."},
	"ability":{"title":"CHARACTER ABILITY","text":"J, right mouse, controller RT or ABILITY uses your character's skill. Bram slams nearby ground; Vex lunges and applies bleeding; Aria uses a wide saber sweep; only Lyra fires bullets. Abilities cost energy and recover separately from ordinary strikes. Your character is fixed for the performance."},
	"bleed":{"title":"BLEEDING / SUSTAIN","text":"Vex's blade hits and Razorstep apply up to three bleeding stacks. Each stack deals 3 damage per second for three seconds; another blade hit refreshes it. Lifeline healing instead restores a percentage of direct strike damage, so rapid weak hits cannot multiply a flat healing reward."}
}
